# Regression test for issue #2: a bare invalid escape as the very first
# character of a here-doc body must be rejected. This previously slipped
# through even after the general fix, because the mode switch to Heredoc
# happened after the lexer had already tokenized this position under the
# ambient Shell mode (via lookahead needed to detect the `-` strip marker
# and the indented body).
let s = |
  \n
# error: only \$ and \\ escapes are valid in here-docs
#   --> heredoc_bad_escape_first_char.dol:LL:LL
#    |
# LL |   \n
#    |   ^^
